# QA M6 regression (was qa_m6_bug_checkpoint_left_into_traun; fixed by
# D-102, E42): holding LEFT after the Bad Ischl checkpoint respawn must not
# walk Resi into the Traun (the M4 "holding LEFT after a checkpoint
# respawn" class; Strobl was designed against it, D-097 addendum item 4).
# bad_ischl_checkpoint's inputs to its death in file B (1266) and the
# respawn at the Esplanade checkpoint (col 152, x 2434, 1326, camera x
# 2296). Then LEFT is held. The bug: she walked left along the landing
# 147-151 and dropped into landing notch 2 (cols 143-146, lethal
# salzach_water) at 1403, 77 frames after the respawn, again at the next
# respawn, then game over. Since D-102 a stone kerb at (151, row 14),
# directly left of the checkpoint, stops her on the landing. Inputs
# unchanged (bad_ischl_checkpoint's prefix is a frozen copy of the pre-E42
# solver route, which the re-solve changed from frame 918 on).
# Expected: a respawned Resi who holds LEFT is stopped on solid ground
# (x >= 2352) and does not die.
level  = bad_ischl
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=1 dies_at frames=1266..1266 lives=2 state=playing player_x>=2352 no_event=GameOver
